Z||000000||Eddie||11-17-1999||08:50 PM||||I remember that year my sister told me a new car was out it was called the FIERO and asked me to go look at one with her she loved it!I was 16 then and my DAD god rest his sole. was just about to finish work on a 1969 firebird for me. It had a 455cub.inch motor in it with a 4 speed trans 10 bolt not a 12 a 10 bolt possie rear in it. And it was fast so what would I see in a fiero at that time nothing.my sister still has that little red fiero.my firebird was wrecked in two years my older brother came home on leave for a week and whent out with it and wrapped up around a tree that was all I had left of him my dad that is.he never had any money but what he had gave to the 7 of us I am wrighting this because every time I go by my sisters and see that fiero I could see him trying to get in that car all six foot four of him one hand on the ground one on the roof he wanted to drive that car so bad but his legs were to bad and could no longer bend THEM he told if he could just drive that car one time he would be so happy that it looked like lots of fun he was right Ill never let mine go Ill keep it just for him . RIP DAD||||reg||6
Z||000001||87GT||11-17-1999||08:56 PM||||The year 1984.  I was beginning my kindergarten year at San Antonio Elementary.  I dont remember too much of '84.  The one thing that I do remember about '84 is that is the year my mother lost a baby boy during delivery. I remember the funeral very well as a matter of fact. I remember leaning up against my dad's Audi at the cemetary.  Ahh, the year 1984.   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||11-17-1999||09:42 PM||||1984 was the BEST year of my life (so far!). I graduated High School in 83 and had a year to kill before I had to go to boot camp training in Orlando, FL in may of 85. Worked part time at a supermarket with a alot of friends and we'd party our asses off every night possible! Had no cares nor worries,  except who was paying for the beer and what was she going to look like in the morning!! Little did I know till 94 when I bought my first Fiero how 1984 would mean even more to me now! The year my all-time favorite car was made!! YES, 84 LIVES AND RULES!!||||reg||6
Z||000003||GT Bastard||11-17-1999||09:55 PM||||1984..... I was 4 years old, so I recall very little. Life was but a dream.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||11-17-1999||10:30 PM||||George Orwell wrote a book about 1984 didn't he? I guess that I should have read it to see if he mentioned the Fiero. The book was so far ahead of its time, so it seems only fitting that he would have wrote about the futuristic little plastic two-seater! Oh, well- I was 14 and full of hormones and had the big "poofy" 80's hair do. If only I could have talked my dad into buying that Indy pace car and keeping it in the barn until now. . .||||reg||14
Z||000005||Racer 1||11-18-1999||02:29 AM||||Back in 84' I was playing with my GI.JOE F-14 tomcat jet 2 seater it was sweet folding wings and pop out landing gears. And playing with my trans formers. I still have my trans formers worth a hell of alot of money now hehe. And sometime around then is when I first learned how to played "Doctor" with this chic across the street. Didnt know a darn thing about fiero's. Jeff ward was riding dirtbikes back then Rick johnson also two of my favorites. !!OH yeah duck and cover in school when the nuclear bomb hit!!<P>I have a original Transformer Optimus prime with box there going for $500+ used.<p>[This message has been edited by Racer 1 (edited 11-18-1999).]||||reg||14
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||11-18-1999||02:54 AM||||in 1984 I was 4 years old and had never heard of the Fiero.. didn't hear about it until I read a "3 Investigators" book in 1991 in fact. One of the characters had a "beat up old Fiero coupe". so I asked my dad.. "what's a Fiero?" So for 8 years (and counting..) I've wanted one. that's my story.<P>not that anyone probably wanted to hear it.. oh well.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||four50four||11-18-1999||06:58 AM||||i don't remember much of 1984, considering that was the year i was born!||||reg||1
Z||000008||DJRice||11-18-1999||08:20 AM||||Well, I was in the 4th grade in '84.  My dad bought a new Buick Lesabre that year, which I just retired about 2 months ago after 249K.<P>Van Halen had a new album, but I wouldnt get into that for some years yet.<P>I also had the GI JOE F-14 with the ejector seat and the transformers.  I still have them all, packed up tightly.<P>My first Fiero would be a 1984.<P>Not a bad year indeed.||||reg||1
Z||000009||87GT||11-18-1999||06:59 PM||||I think its funny here that most of us in 1984 had no earthly idea of what a fiero was.  I was only 5 going on 6 that year so its mostly a blurr to me. I do also have transformers somewhere. I didnt know they were worth something.. I even have a transformers movie!  Cool.||||reg||1
Z||000010||batboy||11-18-1999||09:00 PM||||Ah...kids! In 1984, I had already been out of the military for 5 years, was working my way through college, tearing around in a 1968 Chevelle SS 396, and drooling over the brand new Pontiac Fiero (even though there was no way I could ever afford a new car back then). I still have two Car and Driver magazine articles about the car from that era.<P>Eddie, that was a nice, but kind of sad story about your dad.||||reg||1
