Z||000012||Scott2M4||11-19-1999||07:12 AM||||Very nice story, Eddie.  Quite touching ...<P>I'm up there with you, Batboy.  In 1984, I was in my sophomore year of high school, tooling around in a 1977 Vette ... OK, OK, CHE-vette ... dreaming about girls and cars (what else was important back then!?)<P>I still remember the ad I had that showed the 1984 Fiero with the red body panels ripped from the space frame but hovering close by their resting spots.<P>The car was amazing then and the design, IMHO, has aged quite nicely over the years.||||reg||1
Z||000013||RZURCTN||11-19-1999||08:31 AM||||1984?  I was ten.  What do you do when you're only ten?  Run wild a$$ed through the woods.  Talk about your older brothers piece of junk Toyota Corona Mark II station wagon with your best friend, then go for a swim at the ol' waterin' hole.  I really like the 84 Fiero.  The only year I've ever owned. Wish I never got rid of my first one.  ||||reg||7
Z||000014||2M4 Dale||11-19-1999||09:00 AM||||1984...Went bankrupt in '84. Had crappy job in '84. I was driving a 69' GTO Judge and a 70' GTO. My father-in-law bought a brand new Fiero/silver/coupe. Loved it then. Goats are gone-Fiero is in the garage.||||reg||1
Z||000015||ChadMan||11-19-1999||09:01 AM||||I was 13 in 1984, and I loved Fieros.  Seemed like they were everywhere - you couldn't leave the house without seeing a white or red Coupe.  My transportation was a BMX bike, but I swore I'd have a Fiero when I could afford one.<P>Seems like we've got a lot of Fiero enthusiasts on this forum who are college-aged or younger, which is cool.  Our club has members ranging from 17 to late 60's.||||reg||1
Z||000016||deceler8||11-19-1999||10:15 AM||||I was 24...I remember I was with my dad looking at cars for my younger sister and there was a Fiero on the showroom floor so I got in...really cool looking and fit like a glove...<P>Last year when I started my own business and really didn't need to drive to work anymore I decided I wanted that Fiero I could never afford when they first came out. Especially now that I'm past that age when insurance would be a problem.<P>1984 was a really great year now that you mention it.||||reg||10
Z||000017||Trixi||11-19-1999||11:00 AM||||In 1984 I was four years old.  It was the year that my family got it's very first, brand new car. It wasn't a Fiero though, it was a Ford Tempo GL.  She was a great car, we had her for almost 8 years, then she went to my older brother who finished her off.  She now sits in a wreck in my parents yard. She was a good car.  <P>In 84 I didn't know what a Fiero was, it was a car!  Now I know better!  My fiancee and I recently bought an 84, 4-speed, and I didn't want it.  Then I drove it.  Now I love it!  She's 15 years, I hope she lasts another!||||reg||7
Z||000018||Dan87GT||11-19-1999||01:23 PM||||yea, I remember getting my '84 Fiero in late 1983, what a year, but then I also remember changing the clutch in '85, '86 etc, and putting out an engine fire with a bottle of Mountain Dew, but I still have the car.||||reg||1
